240 - 80 = 160 160 - 60 = 100 1. First, find the number of Chinese participants: 2. Find the number of girls on the Chinese team:

The problem states there were 240 Asian participants, with 80 being Japanese. To find the number of Chinese participants, subtract the number of Japanese participants from the total number of Asian participants: 240 - 80 = 160.  So there were 160 Chinese participants.  We are given that 60 of the Chinese participants were boys. To find the number of girls on the Chinese team, subtract the number of boys from the total number of Chinese participants: 160 - 60 = 100.  Therefore, there were 100 girls on the Chinese team.

\boxed{100}

